alfe needs to pass an empty dwg to bricscad and autocad.  To avoid
reusing previous empty.dwg files, that may be modified or locked by
other instances alfe must create a new empty.dwg file for each
invocation of the CAD, in the invocation workdir.  Eventually we
should have resources and documents and templates, in
/opt/local/share/clautolisp/*/ but for alfe it may be preferable to
keep it stand alone, and since empty.dwg is small, to include it as a
resource in the lisp image.

The following can be used load the empty.dwg file contents into a
vector kept in the lisp image, and to save a copy into a new file when
and where it will be needed. (adjust the "empty.dwg" path for
load-time reading when compiling the source file.

Move the empty.dwg file from issues/open to the right directory
(eg. along with the sources that load it).



#+begin_src lisp
    (defvar *empty-dwg-contents*
      (load-time-value
       (let ((sequence))
         (with-open-file (in "empty.dwg"  :element-type '(unsigned-byte 8))
           (read-sequence (setf sequence (make-array (file-length in)
                                                     :element-type '(unsigned-byte 8)))
                          in))
         sequence)))

    (defun save-empty-dwg (path)
      (with-open-file (out path :element-type '(unsigned-byte 8)
                           :direction :output
                                :if-exists :supersede
                                :if-does-not-exist :create)
        (write-sequence *empty-dwg-contents* out)))
#+end_src

